      "title": "Assistant Vice President of University Advancement /Chief Development Officer",
      "description": "Department: Eastern Illinois University: University Advancement  Location: Charleston, IL Posted: Oct 28, 2026 Eastern Illinois University invites applications for the role of Assistant Vice President (AVP)/Chief Development Officer. Reporting to the Vice President for Student Affairs & University Advancement, this new position is a cornerstone of our advancement division and will serve as a pivotal member of the Advancement Leadership Team as we launch a micro-campaign for our new Integrated Science Building, Admissions Welcome Center, and a renovated residence hall. The AVP will lead the fundraising team and the Strategic Communications & Operations area with a focus on unified institutional priorities, development planning and goal setting, data management, strategic partnership both in Advancement and with other key stakeholders, pipeline development, and securing philanthropic support for colleges and units across EIU. The University and Community: Celebrating more than 130 years of excellence, Eastern Illinois University (EIU) is a fully accredited, comprehensive regional residential institution located in Charleston, Illinois—ideally positioned between Chicago, St. Louis, and Indianapolis. The University is known for its individualized attention, supportive relationships, and exceptional outcomes, including high graduation, retention, and career placement rates. Academically, EIU combines personalized learning with nationally respected programs. Small class sizes allow for close mentorship from distinguished faculty, while innovative undergraduate and graduate programs and firsthand opportunities prepare students for meaningful professional and personal growth. Campus life at EIU is vibrant and community oriented. The University features more than 50 buildings within walking distance, extensive recreational facilities, and more than 200 student organizations including NCAA Division I athletics, and 20+ fraternities and sororities. Cultural life thrives at the world-renowned Doudna Fine Arts Center and the Tarble, which bring exceptional artistic and performance experiences to campus and the region. Students, faculty, and staff enjoy the close-knit atmosphere of a classic college town with convenient access to shops, dining, and outdoor recreation—alongside robust service opportunities coordinated through EIU’s Office of Civic Engagement and Volunteerism. With its strong alumni network, sustainability efforts, and deep commitment to student success, Eastern Illinois University offers an exceptional environment to live, learn, and work. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Manage a portfolio of high-capacity prospects to qualify, cultivate, solicit, and steward principal gifts ($250,000+) Supervise, coach, and mentor a team of fundraising professionals; establish clear annual KPIs and performance metrics that foster a high-output, collaborative culture in partnership with the Vice President for Student Affairs & University Advancement Serve as a key architect for EIU’s annual fundraising plan, micro-campaigns, and upcoming comprehensive campaign Serve as a primary advisor to Deans and other academic leaders Provide strategic guidance on fundraising priorities and donor engagement and translating unit-specific priorities into actionable fundraising initiatives Direct collaboration with Alumni Relations to support Alumni Engagement as well as the Foundation Collaborative relationship with Assistant Athletics Director/Development Responsible for establishing annual fundraising goals and KPIs for Development and individual fundraisers Utilize data analytics to monitor portfolio health, ensuring a fluid \"moves management\" process across the entire frontline team Ensure all fundraising activities align with the university’s strategic plan and centralized advancement standards Partner with Engagement, Communications, and Stewardship teams to ensure seamless donor experience and consistent institutional messaging Represent the university at high-level meetings, events, and individual visits with alumni, friends, and community stakeholders Responsible for managing development’s annual budget Other duties as assigned Work Hours: Standard office hours are 8:00am - 4:30pm Starting Salary/Pay Rate Range: Current annual salary range for this position is $115,000 – $120,000 Application Review will Begin on: November 13, 2026 Start Date (if applicable): December 01 , 2026 Benefits Overview: Eastern Illinois University is proud to offer an excellent benefits package designed to support our employees' well-being and career goals. This position is eligible for the following benefits: Comprehensive Medical Coverage: Competitive employee insurance premiums with flexible plan options. Vision Insurance : Vision coverage is included with medical at no cost. Dental Insurance: Dental plans are available to meet your needs. Retirement Benefits : Participation in the State University Retirement System, which includes medical insurance benefits upon retirement. Tuition Waivers: Opportunities to pursue educational goals through tuition waivers for employees and dependent children. Generous Paid Time Off : Up to 12 paid holidays annually, plus earned vacation and sick time. For more information on our employee benefit programs for this specific position class, please visit EIU Employee Benefits. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited post-secondary institution A minimum of five years of professional fundraising experience in higher education or a nonprofit organization Demonstrated success in qualification, cultivation, solicitation, and closure of six- or seven-figure gifts (or higher) Experience with CRM software (e.g., Raiser’s Edge, Blackbaud CRM, Salesforce) Ability to travel to meet with donors and work evening/weekend events as required Excellent communication, negotiation, and presentation abilities Experience working in a collaborative, team-oriented environment Demonstrated ability to positively represent EIU in visits with alumni, donors and constituents Supervisory experience Strong commitment to the Donor Bill of Rights and the ability to maintain the highest levels of confidentiality Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree or relevant campaign experience Experience leading or mentoring professional staff in a goal-oriented setting Goal setting and tracking experience Experience in determining appropriate gift levels and writing effective gift proposals Working knowledge of or experience with major gift fundraising, annual giving, and corporate and foundation fundraising Raiser’s Edge NXT or Blackbaud CRM experience Campaign experience Three years or more experience as a supervisor Demonstrated success in closing principal-level gifts ($250,000+) Applicants must submit a cover letter, resume, transcripts, and contact information for three references to https://apply.interfolio.com/196561. Questions about the application process should be directed to Nancy R. Murray, Screening Committee Chair, nrmurray@eiu.edu. Applicants with disabilities are encouraged to apply and may request a reasonable accommodation under the Americans with Disabilities Act to complete the application and/or interview process. If would like to request assistance with the application/interview process, please contact Human Resources at (217) 581-3911 or employment@eiu.edu for assistance."
    }
